    How many apps does it take to run a creative agency? Depends, what do you need to do? Find clients, manage projects, talk to clients, get designs approved, chase payments. So, a lot of apps. Way too many. Your leads are in a CRM. Your projects are in a project management tool. Feedback lives in email or a separate proofing app. Client conversations are somewhere else. And proposals, invoices and payments, more tools. And none of them seem to know what's happening in the others. What if they were all connected? Meet Nod Stage, one connected workspace built around how creative studios actually work. Start with your leads. Manage inquiries, discovery calls, follow -ups and proposals. When a deal is won, turn it into a project. Manage projects, tasks, deadlines and your team's workload. Give clients their own branded portal. Share files and proofs, collect visual feedback, manage revisions and get approvals. Keep conversations and video messages together. Manage your calendar, change orders, invoices and payments. Automate repetitive work, use intake forms and templates, track performance and request testimonials. So I don't need to keep jumping between all those tools. That's the whole point. Less switching, less chasing, one connected workflow. Nod Stage is coming soon. Join the waitlist for early access.
